# The two server-side features: Ask Riz, the chat panel in the header, and the GPU
# finder's model lookups. Copy to `.env.local` for development and set the same keys in
# the Vercel project's environment variables for deployment.
#
# The diagram itself needs none of these. Unset, the app builds, deploys and renders
# exactly as it did before either feature existed: the panel answers that it is not
# configured, and the finder falls back to its cached models and to whatever token the
# reader supplies. Nothing else degrades.

# Required. The panel's only outbound call.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to claude-haiku-4-5, which ties Sonnet 5 at 8/8 on `npm run eval`
# and costs 2.6x less. Anthropic's slugs move faster than this repository does, so this
# is here to avoid a deploy for a model swap -- run the eval before using it.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# Optional. Defaults to 2000. Questions per day across *everyone*, which is the only
# limit that bounds the invoice -- the per-IP windows price abuse rather than cap it,
# since addresses are rented by the thousand. Roughly $59/day at the worst a single
# question can cost on the Haiku default, nearer $30 in ordinary use.
RIZ_GLOBAL_DAILY=

# Required in production, ignored in development. /api/ask is unauthenticated and sits in
# front of a billed API key, so the route refuses to serve rather than serve unlimited when
# these are missing -- see lib/ratelimit.ts. Vercel's Upstash integration provisions
# KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN instead, and both spellings are read.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# The GPU finder's shared Hub token, read by /api/hub and by `npm run models` when it
# rebuilds the cache. Read-only, and it wants no scope beyond public and gated repos --
# it is lent to every visitor thirty lookups an hour at a time, so anything it can reach,
# they can. Unset, the finder serves its cached models and asks for a token for the rest.
HF_TOKEN=

# Optional. Defaults to 2400. Model lookups per day across *everyone* on the shared token,
# which is what actually bounds its exposure -- the per-IP window is 720/day on its own and
# addresses are not scarce. What runs out here is the Hub account's standing rather than a
# bill, so the failure is everyone's lookups at once. See lib/ratelimit.ts.
HUB_GLOBAL_DAILY=
